  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EmpowerHER</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">High poverty in rural areas in C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire drives various social issues. Despite efforts from the private and public sector and other stakeholders in the agricultural sector, gender inequality and child labour remain key issues on the development agenda. Village Savings and Loans Associations (VSLA) are increasingly seen as promising interventions to contribute to a Living Income and child well-being of resource-poor households in rural areas. Key elements for the success of VSLAs include ease of implementation and access for members without complicated terms or registration procedures. ETG has embedded the VSLA approach in its core sustainability strategy. However, the informal nature of VSLAs is also a limiting factor. Loans taken through VSLAs may cover small farm expenses or school fees during periods of low income but are insufficient for larger entrepreneurial investments. One strategy to increase the social and economic impact of VSLAs is to include them in the formal financial sector and give members access to financial products, including larger amounts of loans, and reduce the risk for Micro Finance Institutes (MFIs).The proposed EmpowHer project is a partnership between ETG and Beyond Beans. Micro fiance institute Advans will conduct a thorough financial assessment of the selected VSLAs to assess their credit score. At the same time Community Based Organisations (CBO&apos;s)  will assess the organizational capacity of the VLSAs and income situation of its members. Beyond Beans will identify the scope of technical support needed for the selected VSLAs to include them in the financial sector. In addition, the financial partners will identify and/or develop financial products that can be offered to VSLAs.</narrative>
  </description>
